# `-d remote` only — the CHUNK_REMOTE-backed maker app on the Unraid box (Arc D Task 2), syncing
# against the standalone `sync` accessory (config/deploy.yml).
# Read as [.kamal/secrets-common, .kamal/secrets.remote]; .kamal/secrets (base) is NOT read.
# Safe for git: references and commands only, never a raw credential.

# SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN — the operator credential FileLayer::ChunkRemote::Provisioning sends on this
# app's own admin call to POST /v1/admin/libraries, auto-provisioning a library the first time a
# user with no `sync_device_token` yet touches their files (app/services/file_layer/chunk_remote/
# provisioning.rb) — AND required at BOOT by LibraryBackendCheck.check_chunk_remote! (lib/
# library_backend_check.rb): without it this deployment cannot provision a library for ANY user, so
# the guard refuses to start rather than booting clean and FetchError-ing on someone's first write.
# MUST resolve to the IDENTICAL value the `sync` accessory's own SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN resolves to
# (config/deploy.yml) — both sides read this SAME 1Password item/field, which is what GUARANTEES
# the match rather than merely hoping two independently-typed values agree. A mismatch does not
# fail loudly: Sync::V1::Admin::LibrariesController#authenticate_admin! on the far side (chaim354/
# tinkerex-sync) just 503s "admin provisioning disabled", which reads as a config gap rather than a
# wrong credential.
#
# NEVER .kamal/secrets-common (§14g): that file's `$(…)` lines are evaluated EAGERLY for every
# destination that reads it, and share/s3/ovh/chunk have no use for this credential — this app
# never calls the admin door except when LIBRARY_BACKEND=chunk_remote. The other four destinations
# DO each carry their own reference to this same item (see .kamal/secrets, .kamal/secrets.share,
# .kamal/secrets.s3, .kamal/secrets.ovh) — not because their containers send it, but because the
# `sync` accessory that DOES need it lives in the shared, never-overlaid config/deploy.yml
# `accessories:` block, so it is a required key on every destination's MERGED config regardless
# (verified against Kamal::Configuration.raw_config, not assumed). This file is the one copy that
# is functionally exercised: it is what lets THIS container's own admin HTTP call succeed.
SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN=$(bin/secret SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN 'op://tinkerex/tinkerex-sync-admin-token/password')

# CHUNK_REMOTE_TOKEN IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT FROM THIS FILE. It was Stage 4's per-request device
# credential and LibraryBackendCheck.CHUNK_REMOTE_REQUIRED demanded it at boot for a while after
# nothing in app/ or lib/ read it any more (Arc C moved that job to per-user `users.sync_device_token`,
# provisioned lazily via SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN above) — a stale rule fixed in the same commit that removed
# it from CHUNK_REMOTE_REQUIRED's definition (that constant's own comment has the full history). It
# survives only as a LOCAL dev/CI credential (config/ci.rb's readiness probe, bin/sync-server, both
# minting and checking a real device against an ephemeral local server) — not a deployment concern.
# Do not re-add a reference here on the strength of finding it still used in those two files.
